{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkLpmPFYb92VqVhd2JSv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't changed anything yet. I can't look up the commit SHA for `actions/checkout@v4` from here, and I won't guess one. A made-up or misremembered SHA would break the workflow, or pin it to a commit you didn't intend.\n\n`.github/workflows/deploy.yml` is the only workflow, and it has one action to pin:\n\n```yaml\n- uses: actions/checkout@v4\n```\n\nRun this to get the SHA that `v4` currently points to:\n\n```bash\ngh api repos/actions/checkout/commits/v4 --jq .sha\n```\n\nSend me the output and I'll make the edit. I'd write it as `uses: actions/checkout@<sha> # v4`, so Dependabot or Renovate can keep updating the pin. If you can run commands in this session, I can do the lookup and the edit myself.\n\nI also noticed two security problems in the same file:\n- **Script injection:** `echo \"Title is ${{ github.event.pull_request.title }}\"` puts the PR title straight into a shell command. Anyone who can open a PR can run commands in the job. The fix is to pass it through `env:` and reference `\"$PR_TITLE\"`.\n- **Excessive permissions:** `permissions: write-all` gives the token write access to everything. That is especially risky on a `pull_request` trigger, where the injection above can reach it. `contents: read` is probably enough.\n\nI haven't touched either of these, since you only asked for pinning. I can fix them in the same edit if you want."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":286,"cache_read_input_tokens":12488,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":286},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"083b53dc